WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Dr. Khalifa: ... (unintelligible)

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, if I (unintelligible), you have the choice, I mean, to agree with it or disagree with it.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000
And when you express an opinion, you may convince me of changing my opinion, or I may choose not to take your opinion.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:26.000
So, the purpose of reading Al-Fãtehah is for Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala to guide us to see the truth and to remain as brothers, whether the difference between us or not.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
And I'm hoping that the people who hate me this morning will love me at the end of their (unintelligible)

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Because I love them (unintelligible). I'm happy.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.000
I know you're sincere.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
And I know that most people who go to the mosque or church will break God's law.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
We're all Muslims, and I love you for it.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.000
You are very enthusiastic, and I love you for it.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
And I hope at the end, we will be brothers.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.000
I may have a different opinion than you. You may have a different opinion than mine.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.000
But I'm convinced, and I really mean it, that you are sincere people.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:03.000
And I love you are here, and not in a nightclub, or watching a dancer, or breaking God's law in any way.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.000
You'll never break God's law. I know that you follow the Quran.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.000
So, and I grew up in the same conditions as you.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.000
I passed through the same stages that you're passing through.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.000
And we change, people change, because we learn, otherwise there is no use.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Every day that we don't learn something, and we change a little bit, is not worth living.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:31.000
So, we're going to read Al-Fãtehah now, and we sincerely turn to Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala to guide us to the truth.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.000
Guide me to the truth, and guide you to the truth.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.000
And we'll be sincere, IN SHAA ALLAH, in reciting Al-Fãtehah.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.000
For only Quran says Eyyaka Na’abudu Wa Eyyaka Nasta’aeen (1:5)

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.000
Al-Fãtehah

00:01:41.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem (1:1) Al hamdu Lillahi Rabbil ‘Alameen (1:2) Arrahman Arraheem (1:3) Maliki Yawm Eddeen (1:4) Eyyaka Na’abudu Wa Eyyaka Nasta’aeen (1:5) Ehdina Al-Serata Al-Mustaqeem (1:6) Serata Al-Lazeena An’amta ‘Alayhim Ghayri Al-Maghdoobi ‘Alayhim Wa Laddaalleen (1:7)

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.000
Alhamdu Lillah

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.000
In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Praise be to God.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Wa Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.000
And I bear witness that there is no god except the One God.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Wahdahu La Shareeka Lah

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.000
He alone is God. He has no partners.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.000
Our topic this morning is, why...

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.000
This is Canada, North America, the folks say anything they want.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.000
This is not Egypt or Iraq, or any other place.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.000
They say anything they want.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.000
The topic this morning is (unintelligible) or the reason why we are here.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.000
"Why are we here? What is our objective?"

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:58.000
Are we here to go to school and get a degree, and make a lot of money, and build a big house, and have a beautiful wife, and a lot of children?

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.000
Are we here for this, to make a lot of money, and have a nice home, be respectful to society?

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.000
What are we here for?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:15.000
The teacher, Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala, in the Quran, teaches us, tell us why we are here.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:20.000
In Sura Al-Dhãreyãt, number 51, Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala says,

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.000
(51:56) وَمَا خَلَقْتُ ٱلْجِنَّ وَٱلْإِنسَ إِلَّا لِيَعْبُدُونِ

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.000
These are two negatives.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:30.000
[51:56] I did not create the humans and the jinns except to worship Me alone.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.000
That's what Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala said.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:34.000
So, that is the purpose of, of us being here.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:41.000
But what we forget to remember is that we have an archenemy.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:49.000
You and I have a common enemy that we must band together against, instead of fighting with each other.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:54.000
And this archenemy, that is your enemy and my enemy, is called Iblis (Satan).

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.000
He swore by God's Majesty.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.000
(38:82) فَبِعِزَّتِكَ لَأُغْوِيَنَّهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.000
"I swear by Your Majesty, I will deceive them all."

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.000
(38:83) إِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنْهُمُ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:12.000
The only people who can escape the grip of Iblis (Satan) are the people who are totally devoted Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.000
(38:83) إِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنْهُمُ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.000
Iblis swore that he will come from in front of us, from behind us, from our right and our left.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:29.000
لَـَٔاتِيَنَّهُم مِّنۢ بَيْنِ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ وَعَنْ أَيْمَـٰنِهِمْ وَعَن (7:17) شَمَآئِلِهِمْ ۖ وَلَا تَجِدُ أَكْثَرَهُمْ شَـٰكِرِينَ

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.000
[7:17] "... You will find that most of them are unappreciative."

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.000
of You.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:47.000
Satan (Iblis), unfortunately, succeeded to a great extent.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:50.000
And this is recorded in the Quran, and we see it in life.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:57.000
Of all the followers of Jesus Christ, how many billions follow him as he really wants to be followed?

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:02.000
How many Christians believe that Jesus is a messenger of God?

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:06.000
And how many believe that he's son of God, or God, or part of the Trinity?

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.000
How many of them love Jesus, of the Christians?

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:12.000
This is what Iblis did to them.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:22.000
Iblis convinced them that they love Jesus so much that he must be greater than a human being and a messenger of God.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:29.000
Satan came to them from their right, from their left, from their front, from their back.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.000
And you see the results.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:34.000
You and I agree on the results of what happened to the Christians.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.000
You and I agree on what happened to the Jews.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.000
First, he made them disrespect their prophets.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.000
They killed their prophets.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
They have no respect for Moses.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:50.000
They have no respect for any of the prophets. And historically, as recorded in the Quran, the Jews killed their prophets.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.000
They have absolutely no respect for them.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:59.000
But Satan, Iblis, turned around and he made them reverence and worship their scholars.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.000
(9:31) ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟ أَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَـٰنَهُمْ أَرْبَابًۭا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:07.000
They set up their rabbis and their priests as gods beside God.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.000
How?

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:13.000
The Ahbar (أَحْبَار) and the Rohban (رُهْبَـٰنَ),

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:18.000
the rabbis and the priests wrote for them the Talmud,

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:24.000
which is divided into two parts, Mishnah which means Hadith and Gemarrah which means Sunna. This is the Talmud.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:27.000
(unintelligible)

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:34.000
The Talmud is now followed by the Jews, not the Torah. They do not follow the Torah. They follow the Talmud.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.000
Iblis succeeded with the Jews and misled them.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.000
(9:31) ٱتَّخَذُوٓا۟ أَحْبَارَهُمْ وَرُهْبَـٰنَهُمْ أَرْبَابًۭا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:47.000
They, they set up their religious scholars as gods besides God.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:52.000
And they take the words of God, the Torah.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:57.000
With the Christians, Satan misled them by the millions.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:02.000
I mean, you can stand here and say "are those millions upon millions of Christians wrong and you are right?"

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.000
You can say that.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.000
And of course, they are wrong.

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:07.000
And it's because of Iblis.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:10.000
And because idol worship is very subtle.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.000
أَخْفَى مِنْ دَبِيبِ النَّمْلِ

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.000
Shirk

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.000
If there's an ant crawling in there, you will not see it.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:24.000
And if you hold an idol worship, if I hold an idol worship, we will not see it, unless we resort to the Quran.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:29.000
Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala is The Savior who gives us criteria to detect our idol worship.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:41.000
The Quran teaches us that the Shirk is so hidden, idol worship is so hidden, that you and I swear, by God, that we are not idol worshipers.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:50.000
And until the Day of Judgment, some people will swear by God,

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:53.000
face to face, on the Day of Judgment, that they are not idol worshipers.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.000
(6:22) وَيَوْمَ نَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيعًۭا

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:57.000
On the Day, we gather them all.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:02.000
(6:22) ثُمَّ نَقُولُ لِلَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوٓا۟ أَيْنَ شُرَكَآؤُكُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ كُنتُمْ تَزْعُمُونَ

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Then, we say to the idol worshipers, where are your idols now to help you?

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:12.000
(6:23) ثُمَّ لَمْ تَكُن فِتْنَتُهُمْ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُوا۟ وَٱللَّهِ رَبِّنَا مَا كُنَّا مُشْرِكِينَ

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:17.000
Their only answer would be "we swear by God, our Lord, we were not idol worshipers."

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.000
(6:24) ٱنظُرْ كَيْفَ كَذَبُوا۟ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمْ

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:25.000
I mean, I can lie to somebody, I can lie to other people, but lying to myself!?

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.000
They lied to themselves.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:31.000
They told themselves "I am not an idol worshiper."

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:36.000
"I swear by God, my Lord, that I am not an idol worshiper."

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:41.000
And on the Day of Judgment, face to face with Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala, they will swear,

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:44.000
"by God, our Lord, we are not idol worshipers."

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:53.000
We learn in Sura Al-Nahl, Sura 16, verse 22, that what we say with our mouths does not mean a thing.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:09:00.000
I can say "I believe in God, I believe in the Hereafter", but my heart inside may deny that.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.000
(16:22) إِلَـٰهُكُمْ إِلَـٰهٌۭ وَٰحِدٌۭ ۚ

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.000
[2:163] Your god is one god

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.000
(16:22) فَٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ قُلُوبُهُم مُّنكِرَةٌۭ

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:13.000
Those who do not believe in the Hereafter, their hearts inside are denying what they say with their mouths.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.000
(unintelligible)

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:21.000
Well, and how do we know then that we are not idol worshipers?

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:24.000
How do I know that I'm not an idol worshiper?

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:31.000
If it is a fact, and it is a fact because it is mentioned in Quran, that there are people, on the Day of Judgment, who swear

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.000
(6:23) وَٱللَّهِ رَبِّنَا مَا كُنَّا مُشْرِكِينَ

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:37.000
How do I know that I am not one of those people?

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:46.000
There's one way to find out, and that is to wait until the Day of Judgment and then find out.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.000
I go in that group and I say,

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:50.000
وَٱللَّهِ رَبِّنَا مَا كُنت مُشْرِك

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:55.000
And then, I find out that I was idol worshiper and I was unaware.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:59.000
This is one way of finding out, and you will agree with me that it is not the right way.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.000
The other right way, the other way, is to find out now.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:11.000
You and I want to find out if we are worshipping our Creator, who created us or not.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:15.000
(30:40) ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِى خَلَقَكُمْ ثُمَّ رَزَقَكُمْ ثُمَّ يُمِيتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يُحْيِيكُمْ

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.000
[30:40] GOD is the One who created you. ...

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:24.000
God is the One provided for you. God is the One who will terminate your life. God is the One who resurrects you.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:32.000
So, you and I must find out whether we are worshipping our Creator, our Provider, or not.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:39.000
The message of Quran states that it is Allah alone. This is the key that we must worship.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:49.000
That Allah alone will not need any help or assistance or a servant or a king or anything with Him, that we accept Allah alone by Himself.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:53.000
What are the criteria? How do we find out?

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:58.000
The intelligent, first, if I am intelligent, I will put myself on trial.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:01.000
I will say "Rashad Khalifa, you are an idol worshipper, but you don't know."

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:11.000
And I want to prove very hard that I am not an idol worshipper, but first I must accuse myself of being an idol worshipper.

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.000
And you come to me and say "Rashad Khalifa, you're an idol worshipper."

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:18.000
If I am smart, I will say "wait a minute, maybe I am."

00:11:19.000 --> 00:11:24.000
Let us see, let us prove that I am an idol worshipper, until I fail.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:33.000
I must, actually, set out to prove that I am an idol worshipper, and not be convinced until I fail to prove that I am an idol worshipper.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.000
I have to put myself on trial.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:39.000
We must hold ourselves accountable here.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:46.000
And we have the book that will teach us how to find out.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:52.000
There are criteria in the Quran. This is why one of the names of the Quran is Al-Furqãn.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:58.000
It provides criteria to tell us "am I an idol worshipper or not?"

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.000
I have to assume that I am.

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:02.000
(unintelligible)

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:07.000
Because we are free in this world to say anything. We are free to believe in anything.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:12.000
And this is our chance to correct any error or any mistake that you may fall in.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:20.000
The first criterion, we find in Sura Al-Zumer.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.000
Sura 39, verse 45.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.000
And here's the criterion, it says,

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.000
وَإِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:32.000
When God alone is mentioned,

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:35.000
ٱشْمَأَزَّتْ قُلُوبُ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.000
The heart of those who do not believe in the Hereafter... remember the verse?

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.000
(16:22) ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ ... قُلُوبُهُم مُّنكِرَةٌۭ

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.000
Their hearts are denying.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:48.000
The hearts of those who do not believe in the Hereafter become upset. They become upset.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.000
وَإِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.000
When God alone is mentioned, they become upset.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:58.000
So, I have to ask myself "Rashad Khalifa, you're an idol worshipper", and I want to apply this criterion to you.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:01.000
If God alone is mentioned, do you become upset?

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:02.000
I'm asking myself.

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:13.000
If I am upset, according to this Quranic criterion, because I say "Allah alone", then I must accuse myself of being an idol worshipper.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:17.000
I must be convinced that I am idol worshipper, because the Quran says so.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:24.000
(39:45) وَإِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ ٱشْمَأَزَّتْ قُلُوبُ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:34.000
You have to ask yourself "If someone is talking to me about God alone, without Jesus, Mary, Muhammad, Sayyid Al-Badawī or anyone, am I going to get upset? Am I going to kill this person?"

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.000
"Or what am I gonna do?"

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:40.000
This will, this will show you, what, if you are an idol worshipper or not.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:43.000
Do you conform to this criterion or not?

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.000
This is half the criterion.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.000
The second half says,

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:51.000
(39:45) وَإِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن دُونِهِۦٓ إِذَا هُمْ يَسْتَبْشِرُونَ

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:55.000
When someone else is mentioned with Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala, they become happy.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:58.000
They become content.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.000
This is one criterion.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:16.000
The worship must be devoted to Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala alone, without the necessity of adding

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.000
anything else to Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala.

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.000
So, I have to put myself on trial and apply this criterion.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.000
There's another criterion that conforms with this.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:29.000
In Sura Ghãfer, verses 10 through 12 says,

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:36.000
إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ يُنَادَوْنَ لَمَقْتُ ٱللَّهِ أَكْبَرُ مِن مَّقْتِكُمْ أَنفُسَكُمْ إِذْ (40:10) تُدْعَوْنَ إِلَى ٱلْإِيمَـٰنِ فَتَكْفُرُونَ

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:41.000
Those who disbelieve are called, on the Day of Judgement,

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.000
your abhorrence of your own selves...

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.000
Excuse me.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:54.000
[40:10] ... "The abhorrence of GOD towards you is a lot worse than your abhorrence of your own selves. Because you were invited to

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:57.000
"IMAN, faith, but you refused."

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.000
(40:11) قَالُوا۟ They said

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:07.000
رَبَّنَآ أَمَتَّنَا ٱثْنَتَيْنِ وَأَحْيَيْتَنَا ٱثْنَتَيْنِ فَٱعْتَرَفْنَا بِذُنُوبِنَا فَهَلْ إِلَىٰ (40:11) خُرُوجٍۢ مِّن سَبِيلٍۢ

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:14.000
They say "Our Lord, you gave us two deaths and two lives. Is there any way out?"

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.000
And now we confess our sins.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.000
"Is there any way out?"

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:20.000
Is there any way out of Hell?

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.000
And listen to the answer, please.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:24.000
Listen to the answer.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:28.000
Because this is what I would ask myself to find out if I am one of those or not.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:29.000
The answer is,

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:34.000
(40:12) ذَٰلِكُم بِأَنَّهُۥٓ إِذَا دُعِىَ ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُۥ كَفَرْتُمْ

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:41.000
That is because when God alone is advocated, you disbelieved.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.000
(40:12) وَإِن يُشْرَكْ بِهِۦ تُؤْمِنُوا۟

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:46.000
And when you add some other names to Him, you believe.

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.000
(40:12) فَٱلْحُكْمُ لِلَّهِ ٱلْعَلِىِّ ٱلْكَبِيرِ

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:52.000
So, this is the other, this is the number one criterion.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:56.000
"That when God alone is mentioned, I become upset."

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:59.000
This would tell me right away that I am an idol worshipper.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.000
The second criterion.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.000
This...

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:20.000
The second criterion is found ironically in the (unintelligible) other verse, verse 45. Now, I will stop...

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.000
(39:45) وَإِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.000
When God alone is mentioned, the person is upset.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.000
This is in verse 45 of Sura 39.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:32.000
And verse 45 of Sura 17 is the second criterion.

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.000
It says,

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.000
(17:45) وَإِذَا قَرَأْتَ ٱلْقُرْءَانَ

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:38.000
When you read the Quran,

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:41.000
(17:45) جَعَلْنَا بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.000
The same word.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:46.000
We put between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter,

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:48.000
(17:45) حِجَابًۭا مَّسْتُورًۭا

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.000
An invisible wall.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:57.000
When you read the Quran, we put between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter, an invisible wall.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.000
(17:46) وَجَعَلْنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمْ أَكِنَّةً أَن يَفْقَهُوهُ

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:13.000
And we put in their, on their hearts, on their minds, shields to prevent them from understanding the Quran.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:17.000
They cannot get one word of Quran.

00:17:17.000 --> 00:17:28.000
Because Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala set out to put a veil on their minds to prevent them, actively prevent them from seeing the Quran.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:38.000
They can be professors of Arabic linguistics in the College of Shari'a, or the College of Arabic Language at the Azhar university, and they cannot get a single word

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:42.000
from the Quran because of what is in their hearts.

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:46.000
Because they, in their hearts, deny what their mouth says that they are believers.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:50.000
(17:45) إِذَا قَرَأْتَ ٱلْقُرْءَانَ When you read the Quran,

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:56.000
(17:45) جَعَلْنَا بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ We place between you and those who do not believe

00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:00.000
(17:45) حِجَابًۭا مَّسْتُورًۭا An invisible wall.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:02.000
(17:46) وَجَعَلْنَا عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمْ أَكِنَّةً أَن يَفْقَهُوهُ

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:09.000
And we place shields on their hearts or minds to prevent them from understanding

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.000
(17:46) وَفِىٓ ءَاذَانِهِمْ وَقْرًۭا

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.000
And deafness in their ears.

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:16.000
It doesn't matter what you say, they cannot hear what you say.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:25.000
And here, here's a very important part of it (unintelligible)

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:33.000
(17:46) وَإِذَا ذَكَرْتَ رَبَّكَ فِى ٱلْقُرْءَانِ وَحْدَهُۥ وَلَّوْا۟ عَلَىٰٓ أَدْبَـٰرِهِمْ نُفُورًۭا

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: When you preach your Lord using the Quran alone,...

00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:43.000
A man: (unintelligible)

