I'm trying to find out if I am an idol worshipper or not.

00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.000
And here is the criterion.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:10.000
(17:46) إِذَا ذَكَرْتَ رَبَّكَ فِى ٱلْقُرْءَانِ وَحْدَهُۥ وَلَّوْا۟ عَلَىٰٓ أَدْبَـٰرِهِمْ نُفُورًۭا

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:14.000
And when you preach your Lord using the Quran alone,

00:19:14.000 --> 00:19:17.000
(17:46) ٱلْقُرْءَانِ وَحْدَهُۥ وَلَّوْا۟ عَلَىٰٓ أَدْبَـٰرِهِمْ نُفُورًۭا

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.000
They turn away in aversion.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:22.000
Some people believe that the word Wadahu (وَحْدَهُ) refers to Rabbaka (رَبَّكَ)

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:27.000
(17:46) وَإِذَا ذَكَرْتَ رَبَّكَ فِى ٱلْقُرْءَانِ وَحْدَهُۥ وَلَّوْا۟ عَلَىٰٓ أَدْبَـٰرِهِمْ نُفُورًۭا

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:35.000
If you preach your Lord alone, in the Quran alone, without anything else besides the Quran, they turn away in aversion. They don't like it.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:35.000
This is my story.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:39.000
If I, I don't like somebody preaching God to me using the Quran alone,

00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:44.000
this would tell me that I'm an idol worshipper and that I don't know that I am an idol worshipper.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.000
I am unaware of being an idol worshipper.

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:49.000
This is what Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala teaches us in Quran.

