(15:9) إِنَّا نَحْنُ نَزَّلْنَا ٱلذِّكْرَ

00:25:39.000 --> 00:25:40.000
(unintelligible) Zikr (ذِّكْرَ)

00:25:40.000 --> 00:25:42.000
(25:29) لَّقَدْ أَضَلَّنِى عَنِ ٱلذِّكْرِ

00:25:42.000 --> 00:25:44.000
He has taken me away from the Quran.

00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:45.000
(25:29) بَعْدَ إِذْ جَآءَنِى

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:46.000
After I (unintelligible) it.

00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:49.000
(25:29) وَكَانَ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنُ لِلْإِنسَـٰنِ خَذُولًۭا

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:54.000
As I said at the beginning of the lecture, it is because of Satan, because of the (unintelligible).

00:25:54.000 --> 00:25:55.000
(25:30) وَقَالَ ٱلرَّسُولُ

00:25:55.000 --> 00:25:56.000
And this is on the Day of Judgement.

00:25:56.000 --> 00:26:00.000
(25:30) يَـٰرَبِّ إِنَّ قَوْمِى ٱتَّخَذُوا۟ هَـٰذَا ٱلْقُرْءَانَ مَهْجُورًۭا

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:03.000
Obviously, there was no Quran before the prophet.

00:26:04.000 --> 00:26:08.000
Obviously, the Quran was rejected by people who received the Quran.

00:26:10.000 --> 00:26:16.000
People who followed the messenger received the Quran and rejected it.

00:26:17.000 --> 00:26:20.000
(25:31) وَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِىٍّ عَدُوًّۭا مِّنَ ٱلْمُجْرِمِينَ

00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:26.000
We thus set enemies against the prophets from among the criminals.

00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:35.000
And this exactly is the verse that is found in the third criterion to find out if I am an idol worshipper or not.

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:44.000
We find that in Sura Al-An 'ãm, number 6, verses 112-116, it says exactly the same words.

00:26:44.000 --> 00:26:46.000
(6:112) وَكَذَٰلِكَ جَعَلْنَا لِكُلِّ نَبِىٍّ

00:26:46.000 --> 00:26:50.000
We set up against every prophet, and this includes the final prophet,

00:26:50.000 --> 00:26:52.000
عَدُوًّۭا enemies

00:26:52.000 --> 00:26:55.000
شَيَـٰطِينَ ٱلْإِنسِ وَٱلْجِنِّ

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:58.000
humans and jinns devils

00:26:58.000 --> 00:27:01.000
يُوحِى بَعْضُهُمْ إِلَىٰ بَعْضٍۢ زُخْرُفَ ٱلْقَوْلِ غُرُورًۭا

00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:07.000
who teach each other some fancy words to mislead.

00:27:08.000 --> 00:27:10.000
And they are taking those words to the prophet.

00:27:11.000 --> 00:27:13.000
وَلَوْ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ مَا فَعَلُوهُ

00:27:14.000 --> 00:27:17.000
Had your Lord willed, they will not have done that

00:27:18.000 --> 00:27:25.000
Why did God will that these enemies of the prophet fabricate lies? Why did He will that?

00:27:25.000 --> 00:27:29.000
(6:113) وَلِتَصْغَىٰٓ إِلَيْهِ أَفْـِٔدَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ

00:27:29.000 --> 00:27:31.000
In the criterion. See? The same words.

00:27:31.000 --> 00:27:33.000
لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:39.000
In order for the minds of those who do not really believe to listen to those fabrications,

00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:41.000
وَلِيَرْضَوْهُ

00:27:41.000 --> 00:27:44.000
and to be happy with them, to accept these fabrications,

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:47.000
وَلِيَقْتَرِفُوا۟ مَا هُم مُّقْتَرِفُونَ

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:52.000
and to really commit what they are supposed to commit. Because there are people who say

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:59.000
"We are Muslims. We believe. I believe in God. I believe in the Hereafter. I believe in the final prophet. I believe in all the messengers."

00:27:59.000 --> 00:28:03.000
But in their mouths, they're denying what their mouths say.

00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:06.000
But they are not even aware. They don't know.

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:20.000
So, these fabrications, Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala wills that they exist in the world, in order to tell us whether I am a real believer or a false believer.

00:28:21.000 --> 00:28:27.000
وَلِتَصْغَىٰٓ إِلَيْهِ أَفْـِٔدَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ وَلِيَرْضَوْهُ (6:113) وَلِيَقْتَرِفُوا۟ مَا هُم مُّقْتَرِفُونَ

00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:34.000
So, how do we know that this has to do with utterances different than the Quran?

00:28:34.000 --> 00:28:38.000
The next verse tells us that, the next Aya says,

00:28:38.000 --> 00:28:40.000
(6:114) أَفَغَيْرَ ٱللَّهِ أَبْتَغِى حَكَمًۭا

00:28:41.000 --> 00:28:45.000
Do I seek other than Allah as a source of wisdom or as a judge?

00:28:45.000 --> 00:28:50.000
(6:114) أَفَغَيْرَ ٱللَّهِ أَبْتَغِى حَكَمًۭا وَهُوَ ٱلَّذِىٓ أَنزَلَ إِلَيْكُمُ ٱلْكِتَـٰبَ مُفَصَّلًۭا

00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:55.000
When He sends down to you this book, fully detailed.

00:28:55.000 --> 00:28:56.000
مُفَصَّلًۭا

00:28:57.000 --> 00:29:01.000
Where do, why do you go to another source? This is what the verse is saying.

00:29:01.000 --> 00:29:06.000
And this is the criterion that tells me whether I am an idol worshipper or not.

00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:08.000
The second criterion told us

00:29:08.000 --> 00:29:09.000
(17:46) ٱلْقُرْءَانِ وَحْدَهُۥ

00:29:09.000 --> 00:29:11.000
This criterion says

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:13.000
(6:114) أَفَغَيْرَ ٱللَّهِ أَبْتَغِى حَكَمًۭا

00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:20.000
Shall I seek other than Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala as a source of wisdom?

00:29:20.000 --> 00:29:22.000
Who sends down to us this book, fully detailed,

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:23.000
مُفَصَّلًۭا

00:29:23.000 --> 00:29:25.000
There is no other translation for the word مُفَصَّلًۭا

00:29:27.000 --> 00:29:32.000
And the verse goes on to say that even Christians and Jews recognize that this book is from Allah, Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala.

00:29:32.000 --> 00:29:38.000
وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَاتَيْنَـٰهُمُ ٱلْكِتَـٰبَ يَعْلَمُونَ أَنَّهُۥ مُنَزَّلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّكَ بِٱلْحَقِّ ۖ فَلَا (6:114) تَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلْمُمْتَرِينَ

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:40.000
The verse before that, by the way, ends by saying,

00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:41.000
(6:112) فَذَرْهُمْ وَمَا يَفْتَرُونَ

00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:46.000
That the commandment to you and to me is to abandon these fabrications

00:29:46.000 --> 00:29:52.000
that are, are done by the enemies of the prophet and they are fancy.

00:29:52.000 --> 00:29:53.000
(6:112) زُخْرُفَ ٱلْقَوْلِ

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:57.000
Dr. Khalifa: And they are called in the Quran as fabrications.

00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:58.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:29:58.000 --> 00:30:04.000
The next verse, the next verse confirms the verse that says that the Quran is Mufassal (مُفَصَّل).

00:30:04.000 --> 00:30:07.000
(6:115) وَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَتُ رَبِّكَ صِدْقًۭا وَعَدْلًۭا

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:11.000
[6:115] The word of your Lord is complete,* in truth and justice. ...

00:30:12.000 --> 00:30:24.000
So, it makes sense that if I believe God when He says that the book is detailed, if I believe God when He says that the book is complete...

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:47.000
There's one more verse that I would like to mention that if you go to any other source besides the Quran, you are setting up another god besides Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala.

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:50.000
This is what the Quran says. This is what Allah says. It says,

00:30:50.000 --> 00:30:52.000
(6:19) قُلْ أَىُّ شَىْءٍ أَكْبَرُ شَهَـٰدَةًۭ

00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:54.000
Whose testimony is best?

00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:55.000
قُلِ ٱللَّهُ

00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:58.000
Say "God's" testimony is the best.

00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:04.000
Let me read the verse so I don't make any mistake.

00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:06.000
Verse, verse 19, Sura 6.

00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:10.000
In the verse it says,

00:31:10.000 --> 00:31:12.000
(6:19) وَأُوحِىَ إِلَىَّ هَـٰذَا ٱلْقُرْءَانُ لِأُنذِرَكُم بِهِۦ وَمَنۢ بَلَغَ

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:13.000
This is what I want to say.

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:20.000
That this Quran, by name, was given to me to preach to you and to whomever it reaches.

00:31:21.000 --> 00:31:23.000
(6:19) أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَشْهَدُونَ أَنَّ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ ءَالِهَةً أُخْرَىٰ

00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:27.000
Dr. Khalifa: You set up other gods besides God.

00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:28.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:31:29.000 --> 00:31:30.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is what I was looking for.

00:31:31.000 --> 00:31:34.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:31:34.000 --> 00:31:36.000
Dr. Khalifa: (6:19) قُلْ أَىُّ شَىْءٍ أَكْبَرُ شَهَـٰدَةًۭ

00:31:37.000 --> 00:31:39.000
Whose testimony is best?

00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:42.000
قُلِ ٱللَّهُ Say "Allah"

00:31:42.000 --> 00:31:45.000
God's testimony is the best.

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:47.000
شَهِيدٌۢ بَيْنِى وَبَيْنَكُمْ

00:31:47.000 --> 00:31:49.000
He's the witness between me and you.

00:31:50.000 --> 00:31:52.000
وَأُوحِىَ إِلَىَّ هَـٰذَا ٱلْقُرْءَانُ

00:31:52.000 --> 00:31:54.000
And I was given this Quran.

00:31:54.000 --> 00:31:55.000
لِأُنذِرَكُم بِهِۦ

00:31:55.000 --> 00:31:57.000
to preach to you with it

00:31:57.000 --> 00:31:58.000
وَمَنۢ بَلَغَ

00:31:58.000 --> 00:31:59.000
and whomever it reaches.

00:32:01.000 --> 00:32:04.000
أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَشْهَدُونَ أَنَّ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ ءَالِهَةً أُخْرَىٰ

00:32:04.000 --> 00:32:06.000
What is the connection with the Quran to this?

00:32:06.000 --> 00:32:14.000
The prophet is told to say "I was given the Quran to preach to you and all the generations after that until the end of the world."

00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:16.000
What's the connection between

00:32:16.000 --> 00:32:18.000
(6:19) أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَشْهَدُونَ أَنَّ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ ءَالِهَةً أُخْرَىٰ

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:26.000
If you set up anything besides this Quran that was given to the prophet to preach to all generations in the world,

00:32:26.000 --> 00:32:28.000
you are setting up another god besides God.

00:32:29.000 --> 00:32:32.000
Who's the answer to say "I do not testify as you do."

00:32:33.000 --> 00:32:35.000
قُلْ إِنَّمَا هُوَ إِلَـٰهٌۭ وَٰحِدٌۭ

00:32:35.000 --> 00:32:38.000
Say "it is only one god."

00:32:38.000 --> 00:32:39.000
He's only one god.

00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:41.000
وَإِنَّنِى بَرِىٓءٌۭ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُونَ

00:32:41.000 --> 00:32:43.000
And I disown anything you say.

00:32:45.000 --> 00:32:49.000
Why is there prophet's oath in the Quran?

00:32:49.000 --> 00:32:52.000
The strongest swearing in the Quran.

00:32:53.000 --> 00:32:57.000
You know, there are many difference of swearing and oath in the Quran.

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:03.000
There's (unintelligible Arabic)

00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:09.000
(unintelligible Arabic)

00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:16.000
There are many, there are many kinds of swearing in the Quran, but the absolute, the most powerful,

00:33:16.000 --> 00:33:21.000
the strongest swearing in the Quran, you find in Sura Al-Haaqqah, Sura 69. There is

00:33:21.000 --> 00:33:23.000
(69:38) فَلَآ أُقْسِمُ بِمَا تُبْصِرُونَ

00:33:23.000 --> 00:33:26.000
[69:38] I swear by what you see.

00:33:27.000 --> 00:33:28.000
(69:39) وَمَا لَا تُبْصِرُونَ

00:33:28.000 --> 00:33:30.000
[69:39] And what you do not see.

00:33:30.000 --> 00:33:32.000
Now, there's nothing stronger than that.

00:33:32.000 --> 00:33:40.000
God, Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala is swearing by what you see, everything you see, and everything you do not see.

00:33:40.000 --> 00:33:42.000
Which means what? I swear by everything.

00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:45.000
This is absolutely the most powerful oath in Quran.

00:33:45.000 --> 00:33:48.000
(69:38) فَلَآ أُقْسِمُ بِمَا تُبْصِرُونَ (69:39) وَمَا لَا تُبْصِرُونَ

00:33:48.000 --> 00:33:50.000
(69:40) إِنَّهُۥ لَقَوْلُ رَسُولٍۢ كَرِيمٍۢ

00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:53.000
[69:40] This (Quran) is the utterance of an honorable messenger.

00:33:54.000 --> 00:33:56.000
(69:41) وَمَا هُوَ بِقَوْلِ شَاعِرٍۢ

00:33:56.000 --> 00:33:58.000
[69:41] It is not the utterance of a poet; ...

00:33:58.000 --> 00:34:00.000
(69:41) قَلِيلًۭا مَّا تُؤْمِنُونَ

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.000
[69:41] ... rarely do you believe.

00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:04.000
(69:42) وَلَا بِقَوْلِ كَاهِنٍۢ

00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:06.000
[69:42] It is not the utterance of a soothsayer; ...

00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:09.000
(69:42) قَلِيلًۭا مَّا تَذَكَّرُونَ

00:34:09.000 --> 00:34:11.000
[69:42] ... rarely do you take heed.

00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:14.000
(69:43) تَنزِيلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَـٰلَمِينَ

00:34:14.000 --> 00:34:17.000
[69:43] A revelation from the Lord of the world.

00:34:17.000 --> 00:34:18.000
(69:43) تَنزِيلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَـٰلَمِينَ

00:34:19.000 --> 00:34:22.000
(69:44) وَلَوْ تَقَوَّلَ عَلَيْنَا بَعْضَ ٱلْأَقَاوِيلِ

00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:29.000
Dr. Khalifa: And if he uttered anything else, he adds any more, Let me read the...

00:34:29.000 --> 00:34:32.000
Dr. Khalifa (Speaking Arabic): (unintelligible) A man (Speaking Arabic): (unintelligible) Na'am (Yes).

00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: لَأَخَذْنَا مِنْهُ بِٱلْوَتِينَ

00:34:34.000 --> 00:34:36.000
A man: (69:45) لَأَخَذْنَا مِنْهُ بِٱلْيَمِينِ

00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:38.000
Dr. Khalifa: (69:45) لَأَخَذْنَا مِنْهُ بِٱلْيَمِينِ (69:46) ثُمَّ لَقَطَعْنَا مِنْهُ ٱلْوَتِينَ

00:34:38.000 --> 00:34:40.000
He would have been fired as a prophet.

00:34:40.000 --> 00:34:42.000
He would have punished him severely.

00:34:44.000 --> 00:34:49.000
(69:46) ثُمَّ لَقَطَعْنَا مِنْهُ ٱلْوَتِينَ (69:47) فَمَا مِنكُم مِّنْ أَحَدٍ عَنْهُ حَـٰجِزِينَ

00:34:49.000 --> 00:34:51.000
None of you can protect him from Me.

00:34:51.000 --> 00:34:55.000
This is the word came out of the final prophet's mouth.

00:34:56.000 --> 00:34:56.000
And he said,

00:34:56.000 --> 00:35:00.000
[69:38] I swear by what you see. [69:39] And what you do not see.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:04.000
[69:40] This is the utterance of an honorable messenger.

00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:06.000
Obviously, the Quran is

00:35:06.000 --> 00:35:08.000
(69:43) تَنزِيلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَـٰلَمِينَ

00:35:08.000 --> 00:35:10.000
[69:40] This is the utterance of an honorable messenger.

00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:15.000
[69:41] It is not the utterance of a poet; rarely do you believe it.

00:35:15.000 --> 00:35:20.000
[69:42] Nor the utterance of a soothsayer; rarely do you take heed.

00:35:21.000 --> 00:35:26.000
This is, this is Allah's announcement that the majority of human beings will not take heed.

00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:29.000
(69:43) تَنزِيلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَـٰلَمِينَ

00:35:29.000 --> 00:35:31.000
[69:43] A revelation from the Lord of the universe.

00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:39.000
And if he got the honorable message, If the honorable messenger uttered any other word, he would be fired as a prophet.

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:42.000
And will, none of you can protect him from Me.

00:35:42.000 --> 00:35:44.000
This is what Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala says.

00:35:46.000 --> 00:35:47.000
A man: (unintelligible)

00:35:53.000 --> 00:35:57.000
A man (Speaking Arabic): (unintelligible)

00:35:57.000 --> 00:35:58.000
Dr. Khalifa (Speaking Arabic): هذا قول الله سبحانه و تعالی (This is what God Almighty says)

00:35:58.000 --> 00:36:00.000
Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:03.000
Dr. Khalifa (Speaking Arabic): (unintelligible) A man (Speaking Arabic): (unintelligible)

00:36:03.000 --> 00:36:05.000
Dr. Khalifa: (39:45) وَإِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ

00:36:06.000 --> 00:36:11.000
Dr. Khalifa (Speaking Arabic): (unintelligible) A man (Speaking Arabic): (unintelligible)

00:36:11.000 --> 00:36:13.000
Dr. Khalifa: Bism Allah Arrahman Arraheem

00:36:13.000 --> 00:36:21.000
وَإِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ ٱشْمَأَزَّتْ قُلُوبُ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِٱلْـَٔاخِرَةِ (39:45) وَإِذَا ذُكِرَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن دُونِهِۦٓ إِذَا هُمْ يَسْتَبْشِرُونَ

00:36:21.000 --> 00:36:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: صدق الله العلیم (God has spoken the truth)

00:36:23.000 --> 00:36:32.000
A man (Speaking Arabic): (unintelligible)

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:37.000
Ray Caton: It was a practice (unintelligible)

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: My only reference is the Quran, of course.

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:52.000
And we find in Quran that all religious practices of Islam, specifically Salat, Zakat, Fasting, and Hajj, all of them came through Ibrahim.

00:36:52.000 --> 00:37:02.000
We find Salat and Zakat coming through Ibrahim in, for example, in many verses, but for example, verse 73 of Sura 21.

00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:10.000
We find the Hajj, the order or commandment to perform Hajj came through Ibrahim.

00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:13.000
(22:27) وَأَذِّن فِى ٱلنَّاسِ بِٱلْحَجِّ يَأْتُوكَ رِجَالًۭا

00:37:13.000 --> 00:37:17.000
This was directed to Ibrahim. And we find it in Sura 22.

00:37:18.000 --> 00:37:26.000
And the Fasting, if you read the verses of Fasting, you see that the Muslims, before Muhammad,

00:37:26.000 --> 00:37:31.000
used to cheat themselves and have intercourse with their wives during the night.

00:37:31.000 --> 00:37:42.000
The initial decree for Fasting prohibited sexual intercourse throughout the month of Ramadan, day and night, When it came through Ibrahim.

00:37:42.000 --> 00:37:49.000
When the Quran came, this was modified, and allowing intercourse during the night of Ramadan.

00:37:50.000 --> 00:37:58.000
So, the verse is very clear saying that you used to cheat your souls by having intercourse with your wives during the night, but now,

00:37:58.000 --> 00:38:01.000
as of now, you may have intercourse with your wives.

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:08.000
So, it's very clear that all religious practices in Islam came to us through Ibrahim.

00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:12.000
And we must remember that Ibrahim is called the father of Islam.

00:38:13.000 --> 00:38:17.000
(22:78) مِّلَّةَ أَبِيكُمْ إِبْرَٰهِيمَ ۚ هُوَ سَمَّىٰكُمُ ٱلْمُسْلِمِينَ مِن قَبْلُ

00:38:17.000 --> 00:38:20.000
This is verse 78 of Sura 22.

00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:23.000
So, what did Ibrahim contribute being the father of Islam?

00:38:23.000 --> 00:38:30.000
We find out by studying Quran carefully that he contributed all religious practices of Islam.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.000
The prophet Muhammad contributed the Quran.

00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:37.000
The Quran came through Muhammad's mouth, and that was his contribution.

00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:46.000
And this is also why at the beginning of Sura Al-Baqarah, number 2, we find that we must believe in what was revealed before the Quran.

00:38:47.000 --> 00:38:53.000
Because among the things revealed before Quran was the practical scripture given to Ibrahim.

00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:57.000
There was no reading or writing in Ibrahim's time.

00:38:57.000 --> 00:39:06.000
Dr. Khalifa: And he was given a practical, mostly practical, scripture consisting of the duties that we practice now in Islam.

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:11.000
Ray Caton: Question number 7.

00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:18.000
Ray Caton: There are two verses in Quran, Sura 60, 7, 8 and 9.

00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:22.000
Sura 5, 85 and 82.

00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:30.000
Ray Caton: Basically, these refer to the believer not trusting the Jews ...

00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: Not befriending the Christians and Jews and so forth.

00:39:34.000 --> 00:39:38.000
Ray Caton: Yes. The question that was asked is

00:39:38.000 --> 00:39:47.000
"whether or not a person who is a believing Muslim should live in a country that is suppressing Islam,

00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:52.000
"and supporting that country by paying taxes, creating business, employment, one thing or another.

00:39:52.000 --> 00:40:00.000
Ray Caton: "Should he stay there, live, or should he move to another better environment, a more Islamic environment?"

00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:12.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, if the person is oppressed and cannot practice his religion, he cannot Pray, he cannot Fast, he cannot give to charity, and cannot go to hajj, he should move on to another place.

00:40:13.000 --> 00:40:15.000
But this is about the only condition.

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:28.000
To say "you shall not befriend Christians and Jews, and that the Quran says so" would be like saying "you shall not Pray, because the Quran says you shall not pray."

00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:33.000
However, if you complete the sentence, it will say "you shall not Pray while drunk."

00:40:33.000 --> 00:40:37.000
And the same with that statement "you shall not befriend the Jews and Christians",

00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:46.000
it should be, the sentence or the statement should be completed as follows "you shall not befriend the Jews and Christians who oppress you and persecute you because of your religion."

00:40:47.000 --> 00:40:51.000
Towards the end of Sura number 60, which you mentioned,

00:40:51.000 --> 00:41:00.000
specifically the Quran says that God does not forbid you from befriending those who do not fight you and do not evict you from your homes.

00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:10.000
So, we must take the total picture in mind, and we must never tell half-truths or half-statements of Quran. It's very dangerous.

00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:17.000
So, we are not, God does not forbid us from befriending the Jews, Christians, or anyone else who do not fight us.

00:41:22.000 --> 00:41:26.000
Dr. Khalifa: What other parts of the question, I have something else to say, I know that.

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:29.000
Ray Caton: It's whether or not a person should stay... Dr. Khalifa: Oh, yes.

00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: About staying in a country, for example, some people say that this country is not Islamic or oppressive,

00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:41.000
talking about the United States, but in my mind, the United States is about the most Islamic country in the world,

00:41:41.000 --> 00:41:47.000
because a person is free to worship God in any way they want,

00:41:47.000 --> 00:41:54.000
to the extent that if you, if you are in Egypt, or Saudi Arabia, or one of those countries, and you

00:41:54.000 --> 00:42:02.000
really speak up for the true Islam, which is upholding Quran, the whole Quran, nothing but Quran, your life is actually endangered.

00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:12.000
So, it seems to me that the United States is a lot more Islamic than Saudi Arabia, by using that measure.

00:42:13.000 --> 00:42:23.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, people who think that this country is oppressing or, or hampering their Islam in any way, they should think twice.

00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:31.000
Ray Caton: Question number eight, what is the importance of three times washing as opposed to wash till clean?

00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:34.000
Dr. Khalifa: Oh, it's not important, there is no specific number.

00:42:35.000 --> 00:42:46.000
The Quran says "O you who believe, when you get up to Pray, wash your faces, your hands to the elbows, wipe your hair, and wash your feet, that's it, there is no specific number of washings.

00:42:47.000 --> 00:42:52.000
Dr. Khalifa: One will do 2, may do, whichever you feel is necessary.

00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:57.000
Ray Caton: Question number nine "does it do any good to pray for the dead?"

00:42:57.000 --> 00:43:07.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, it all depends on the person's deeds, the dead person, whatever he or she did during this life is what counts.

00:43:08.000 --> 00:43:14.000
If the whole world bands together to pray for Abu Lahab, it will not help him one bit.

00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: And if a person is righteous, his righteousness will benefit him.

00:43:24.000 --> 00:43:33.000
Ray Caton: Number eleven, the word Riba (Usury), meaning interest, does this mean excessive interest or just interest?

00:43:34.000 --> 00:43:39.000
Dr. Khalifa: Any interest that is fixed and guaranteed is considered usury, Riba,

00:43:39.000 --> 00:43:45.000
but if it fluctuates as a result of investing, then this is what is Halal, what is alright.

00:43:46.000 --> 00:43:54.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, the key thing here is fixed and guaranteed, this makes it Riba even if it's 1%, 10% whatever.

00:43:57.000 --> 00:44:04.000
Ray Caton: So, while we are on the subject of money, could you expand a little bit on mortgage and insurance?

00:44:04.000 --> 00:44:11.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, the Quran, the Quran is consistent in saying that it is the taking of Riba that is Haram,

00:44:11.000 --> 00:44:21.000
when you take interest, it is Haram, but if you are forced by circumstances to pay interest to anybody,

00:44:21.000 --> 00:44:27.000
you are considered a victim, the Quran considers you a victim, you're not committing a sin.

00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:37.000
There's the overall rule that says "if you are forced by circumstances without being deliberate or malicious, then you are not committing a sin."

00:44:37.000 --> 00:44:40.000
So, if you are forced to pay interest, that is not Haram.

00:44:40.000 --> 00:44:46.000
What is Haram, consistently in Quran, is the taking of Riba, not the paying of Riba.

00:44:48.000 --> 00:44:56.000
Insurance is considered Haram because of many reasons, first of all, it is a game of chance, gambling.

00:44:57.000 --> 00:45:04.000
Second, it indicates lack of knowledge about God, because if you know,

00:45:04.000 --> 00:45:10.000
then you'll know that if you, if you are with God, nothing bad will happen to you, God will take care of you.

00:45:10.000 --> 00:45:12.000
(39:36) أَلَيْسَ ٱللَّهُ بِكَافٍ عَبْدَهُۥ

00:45:12.000 --> 00:45:14.000
[39:36] Is GOD not sufficient for His servant? ...

00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:19.000
And also, insurance indicates lack of confidence in God.

00:45:20.000 --> 00:45:24.000
So, there is more to it than just a game of chance.

00:45:25.000 --> 00:45:31.000
However, if you are forced, again, if you are forced by circumstance without being deliberate or malicious,

00:45:31.000 --> 00:45:37.000
Dr. Khalifa: and you cannot help it, you have to have insurance for some reason, or it is forced on you, then you are not committing a sin.

00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:45.000
Ray Caton: Just to broaden the question a bit more on mortgage, in terms of loans,

00:45:45.000 --> 00:45:55.000
if a person wants to gain more material wealth by expanding his business and goes into debt by borrowing money to expand his business,

00:45:55.000 --> 00:46:03.000
Ray Caton: to the point where you might call it excessive, greedy, is this allowable?

00:46:04.000 --> 00:46:16.000
Dr. Khalifa: If you write down a project that you want to build apartment complex or invest in something, and to do this you have to have a loan of some kind,

00:46:16.000 --> 00:46:24.000
and then, you go to the bank or a friend or anybody, any source of money, and they tell you "you have to pay interest."

00:46:25.000 --> 00:46:33.000
However, if you take the loan, you know that you will make this investment grow and will bring you a lot of income and a lot of money,

00:46:33.000 --> 00:46:40.000
it is perfectly alright that you go ahead and get the loan and invest it and make your money grow and pay the interest,

00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:50.000
because in Sura 16, we see that the Quran very clearly says that the rich believer is better than the weak and poor believer.

00:46:51.000 --> 00:46:56.000
It is in Satan's best interest to keep you, keep you poor

00:46:56.000 --> 00:47:05.000
and unable to further the cause of God in any way, or increase your knowledge in any way, or benefit from God's provisions.

00:47:05.000 --> 00:47:15.000
So, it is perfectly alright if you write down a project that requires a lot of money to be invested, that will make you a lot of money, make you a millionaire, or whatever.

00:47:16.000 --> 00:47:22.000
Dr. Khalifa: It is perfectly alright to get that loan and pay the interest on it, and invest and carry out your project.

00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:26.000
Ray Caton: Next question.

00:47:27.000 --> 00:47:37.000
Ray Caton: The, We're told in the Sunnah religion that ladies cannot attend mosque or touch Qurans while on their menstruation period.

00:47:37.000 --> 00:47:40.000
Dr. Khalifa: No, this is Satan's favorite trick.

00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:48.000
Satan realizes that the woman is three-quarters of the society, because the woman teaches the children, she is a mother,

00:47:48.000 --> 00:47:54.000
and Satan tried very hard to keep the women oppressed and ignorant.

00:47:55.000 --> 00:48:05.000
One good example is the Sunnah religion's way of keeping the women from going to the Jumu’ah prayer, the Friday prayer, for example.

00:48:06.000 --> 00:48:15.000
Even though Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala in Quran says "O you who believe, when the Jumu'ah prayer is due, drop your business and go to the Jumu'ah prayer."

00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:16.000
It says,

00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:17.000
(62:9) يَـٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓا۟

00:48:17.000 --> 00:48:18.000
[62:9] O you who believe, ...

00:48:18.000 --> 00:48:21.000
It doesn't say "O you believing men, or O you men."

00:48:22.000 --> 00:48:30.000
So, Satan, by injecting this Sunnah or Hadith or whatever it is, and succeeding in forbidding

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:37.000
the women from going to Jumu'ah, he kept them ignorant, and also their children

00:48:37.000 --> 00:48:46.000
are kept ignorant, because you go to work from 8 to 5, and you leave the children, your children with their mother at home, and she teaches them.

00:48:46.000 --> 00:48:54.000
So, we had a good example here in Tucson the other day, three Saudi young men came to buy a car,

00:48:54.000 --> 00:49:02.000
and Kathleen told them to come to the Quranic study, and they said "Oh, we know the Quran" and very quite confident.

00:49:03.000 --> 00:49:07.000
And then, she asked one of them "how many Suras are in Quran?" And he didn't know.

00:49:08.000 --> 00:49:16.000
You know, such a basic knowledge of the even the outside appearance of Quran, let alone the inside.

00:49:16.000 --> 00:49:28.000
Dr. Khalifa: And this is a perfect example, a result of that person's mother being ignorant, too ignorant to teach him about Quran, its characteristics and its contents.

00:49:31.000 --> 00:49:34.000
Ray Caton: What is the importance of washing your feet five times a day?

00:49:34.000 --> 00:49:45.000
In the Sunnah religion, we're, we're taught that if a person has made Wudu in the morning and put socks on, it is not necessary to wash your feet again, during the day that is.

00:49:46.000 --> 00:49:51.000
Dr. Khalifa: Well, back to that verse in Sura number 5, verse number 6,

00:49:51.000 --> 00:49:58.000
it says "O you who believe, when you get up for the prayer, wash your faces, your arms to the elbows, wipe your hair, and wash your feet."

00:49:58.000 --> 00:50:07.000
And all we can say is "yes sir." If you are to obey God, and the words that came out of God's messenger,

00:50:07.000 --> 00:50:11.000
you will say "yes sir", and do these four steps, and no more and no less.

00:50:11.000 --> 00:50:16.000
Satan's objective is to make you disobey and deviate from God's orders in any way.

00:50:17.000 --> 00:50:24.000
And Satan succeeded to a great extent with the Muslim masses, most of them have 9 steps of Wudu.

00:50:24.000 --> 00:50:29.000
Even though Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala gives them 4 steps, they have 9 steps.

00:50:29.000 --> 00:50:35.000
So, they better be prepared on the Day of Judgment to answer that question from Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala when He tells them

00:50:35.000 --> 00:50:39.000
"I have given you 4 steps of Wudu, why did you do 9?"

00:50:40.000 --> 00:50:47.000
You better be ready to answer that. Who is the other god that told them to do 9 steps in Wudu instead of 4?

00:50:48.000 --> 00:50:55.000
Because Allah Subhanahu Wa Ta'ala told them 4 steps. There is some other god, whoever it is, who told them to do 9 steps.

00:50:56.000 --> 00:51:01.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, washing the feet is clearly stated in the Wudu, Sura number 5, verse 6.

00:51:03.000 --> 00:51:08.000
Ray Caton: Can Muslims give their organs or blood as donations?

00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:13.000
Dr. Khalifa: Yes, definitely, because the body is not important at all. Once we leave the body,

00:51:13.000 --> 00:51:21.000
the body is like a garment that we are wearing, and if it is going to help another human being, by all means go ahead and do it.

00:51:22.000 --> 00:51:27.000
Just like if you take off your shirt, an old shirt, and you're gonna throw it away,

00:51:27.000 --> 00:51:31.000
then you worry about if somebody is gonna take the sleeve or the collar or what.

00:51:34.000 --> 00:51:35.000
Dr. Khalifa: That's it.

00:51:35.000 --> 00:51:38.000
Ray Caton: And last question is freedom of choice.

00:51:39.000 --> 00:51:40.000
Thank you.

00:51:40.000 --> 00:51:45.000
God tells us that He can guide whom He wants and mislead whom He wants.

00:51:47.000 --> 00:51:54.000
Ray Caton: Why are we created if we don't have, if God already knows what our destiny is?

00:51:54.000 --> 00:52:03.000
Dr. Khalifa: This is a good question. This indicates that God did not create us to see who's gonna believe and who's not, who will not believe.

00:52:05.000 --> 00:52:11.000
Because God knows, God happens to know exactly what every human being is going to do, believe or disbelieve.

00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:20.000
The purpose of our creation here is to, goes back to the time when Satan wanted to be a god besides God.

00:52:22.000 --> 00:52:33.000
And God decided to give Satan a dominion and constituents to prove Satan's incompetence as a god.

00:52:33.000 --> 00:52:42.000
So, the human beings who set up a god besides God, they automatically become members of Satan's kingdom,

00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:48.000
subject to his incompetence and subject to the disasters and problems that go along with that.

00:52:49.000 --> 00:52:56.000
So, we have the absolute freedom of choice. This is one of the conditions

00:52:56.000 --> 00:53:04.000
for providing Satan with constituents, that we are absolutely free to choose God as our god or Satan as our god.

00:53:04.000 --> 00:53:12.000
People who set up other gods besides God are choosing, automatically choosing Satan as their god.

00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:15.000
And we see, we see this in Sura number 36,

00:53:15.000 --> 00:53:18.000
(36:60) أَلَمْ أَعْهَدْ إِلَيْكُمْ يَـٰبَنِىٓ ءَادَمَ أَن لَّا تَعْبُدُوا۟ ٱلشَّيْطَـٰنَ

00:53:18.000 --> 00:53:23.000
[36:60] Did I not covenant with you, O Children of Adam, that you shall not worship the Satan? ...

00:53:24.000 --> 00:53:28.000
So, we are either worshipping God or worshipping Satan.

00:53:28.000 --> 00:53:39.000
And we worship Satan when we support his point of view of having a god besides God, any other idol besides God, proves Satan's point of view.

00:53:39.000 --> 00:53:45.000
Now, once we make our free choice decision to believe or disbelieve,

00:53:45.000 --> 00:53:52.000
only God knows what our hearts have decided, what our innermost convictions are.

00:53:52.000 --> 00:53:57.000
And based on our decision, God will either create circumstances to guide us,

00:53:57.000 --> 00:54:05.000
if we decide to choose him as our god, or will create circumstances to augment our disbelief and our idolworship,

00:54:05.000 --> 00:54:10.000
if we decide to idolize someone else besides God.

00:54:12.000 --> 00:54:14.000
Dr. Khalifa: So, this should answer all the questions, I guess.

00:54:15.000 --> 00:54:16.000
Ray Caton: Yes, thank you very much.

00:54:16.000 --> 00:54:17.000
Dr. Khalifa: You're welcome. Alhamdu Lillah.

